um", "notes": ["Open seat: Joni Ernst (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's Senate seat is open with Joni Ernst retiring, and the contest between Republican Ashley Hinson and Democrat Josh Turek is one of the cycle's closest. Most forecasters call it a Tossup, though one rates it a Democratic lean. Polling averages show Turek narrowly ahead, with a recent Marist survey giving him an eight-point lead, while Republican-leaning pollsters show a tighter or Hinson-favored race.\n\nMarkets, however, price Hinson as slightly favored, and she holds a substantial cash-on-hand advantage despite heavy Democratic outside spending. The state's Republican lean and the open-seat dynamic cut in different directions, leaving the race effectively even with a modest Democratic tilt in the polling evidence.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6012, "margin": 1.25}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5782, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5857, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5846, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.5}]}